<urn:atm:triage:finding/RBP-W3-F002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBP-W3-F002" ;
  triage:title "NullSqliteObservability::emit structurally infallible Result" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-rusqlite/src/lib.rs:74-77: NullSqliteObservability::emit returns Result<(), AtmError> but the implementation is always Ok(()) — structurally infallible. Either simplify the return type to () or add a doc comment explaining the deliberate infallibility (e.g. intentional no-op for test/null contexts, kept as Result to satisfy the trait contract for future real implementations)." ;
